00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:17.800
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Que tal se a gente passar pelo meio e chegar naquele outro caixa?</lang>

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:19.950
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>Do lado de lá? Tá bom.</lang>

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:27.920
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Viu, às vezes me confundo com o troco nesses supermercados.</lang>
<lang pt-BR>Por que eles nunca colocam as moedas nas nossas mãos?</lang>

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:32.220
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>Porque as moedas caem das maquininhas que ficam ao lado do caixa.</lang>

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:40.500
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Ah, tá... é que nos supermercados brasileiros a</lang>
<lang pt-BR>gente recebe todo o troco dos próprios caixas.</lang>

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.530
<v Orlando>There you go.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:45.170
<v Orlando>That is our dialogue for lesson number two.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:50.759
<v Orlando>As always, we invite everybody to go to the website, <lang pt-BR>Tá</lang>
<lang pt-BR>Falado</lang>, BrazilPod, check out the PDF file, download it,

00:11:50.759 --> 00:11:55.500
<v Orlando>especially this lesson because of that big list
that we made of all the different contractions.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:12:00.448
<v Orlando>Enter the blog, let us know what your
questions are about this lesson so Valdo,

00:12:00.448 --> 00:12:04.190
<v Orlando>Michelle and José Luis and I will
all take some time to answer them.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.300
<v Orlando>With that, lesson number two is done.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.170
<v Valdo>See you next time.

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:07.690
<v Michelle>Bye.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:18.500
<v José Luis><lang pt-BR>Tá Falado</lang>.
